The fix constrains both ends of the range cleanly: --no-merged
HEAD keeps tags we haven't absorbed yet, and --merged origin/HEAD
keeps tags that are on the mainline path. Together they produce exactly
the intermediate checkpoints the loop was designed to walk through.

One edge I noticed: if the repo has tags ahead of origin/HEAD (e.g.,
local tags not yet pushed, or tags on a branch that hasn't landed in
main), those are excluded too. That seems correct -- we don't want to
test-merge into the future -- but worth flagging in case someone has an
unusual local tagging workflow.
